(4984966, 723211, 30982, '<td valign="top">And I was your only comment??  I like this in B&amp;W.  Yeah, it''s pretty in color, but as a B&amp;W kinda gal, I like the way LACK of color emphasizes the structure, the detail.  Oh, and in case you didn''t stop to do the math, it looks like I gave you a 7.  :P</td>', 'And I was your only comment??  I like this in B&W.  Yeah, it''s pretty in color, but as a B&W kinda gal, I like the way LACK of color emphasizes the structure, the detail.  Oh, and in case you didn''t stop to do the math, it looks like I gave you a 7.  :P', '2008-10-01 14:54:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4984969, 724120, 30982, '<td valign="top">In my totally useless opinion, the cuts on the hands and the dirty nails add to the current climate of "fragility" and your title with respect to the country represented by that flag.</td>', 'In my totally useless opinion, the cuts on the hands and the dirty nails add to the current climate of "fragility" and your title with respect to the country represented by that flag.', '2008-10-01 14:55:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(4984977, 724251, 30982, '<td valign="top">The concept is good, but the execution leaves me a little wanting.  It appears to be a handwritten paper sign with an orange on it, which is exactly what I suspect it was.  But you want to make me *think* it''s fancier than that.  Yes, a shadow helps - have MORE of one, but elongated beyond the orange.  Watch the highlights on the surface of the orange itself.  Have a bit of an angle, to get some depth of field to the shot.  It doesn''t feel like a photograph - it feels more like a digital kinda thing where you stuck a picture of an orange in with the letters.  Hopefully some of this is helpful to you - none is meant to be hurtful! I didn''t get this one in voting - to be honest, I''d probably give it a five.  But the folks who liked it REALLY liked it, as you can see by the commenter average!</td>', 'The concept is good, but the execution leaves me a little wanting.  It appears to be a handwritten paper sign with an orange on it, which is exactly what I suspect it was.  But you want to make me *think* it''s fancier than that.  Yes, a shadow helps - have MORE of one, but elongated beyond the orange.  Watch the highlights on the surface of the orange itself.  Have a bit of an angle, to get some depth of field to the shot.  It doesn''t feel like a photograph - it feels more like a digital kinda thing where you stuck a picture of an orange in with the letters.  Hopefully some of this is helpful to you - none is meant to be hurtful! I didn''t get this one in voting - to be honest, I''d probably give it a five.  But the folks who liked it REALLY liked it, as you can see by the commenter average!', '2008-10-01 14:59:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(4985037, 723986, 67152, '<td valign="top">A big congrats Adam on an excellent image.  It just says "Wow!" when you look at it.</td>', 'A big congrats Adam on an excellent image.  It just says "Wow!" when you look at it.', '2008-10-01 15:10:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(4985082, 724388, 71244, '<td valign="top">YO MARIE! congrats to you my friend! wowzers!</td>', 'YO MARIE! congrats to you my friend! wowzers!', '2008-10-01 15:15:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4985230, 723954, 98837, '<td valign="top">my favorite part is the shadow the the eye has in it of the little kid. what color are the eyes? good pic :)</td>', 'my favorite part is the shadow the the eye has in it of the little kid. what color are the eyes? good pic :)', '2008-10-01 16:14:48.000000', NULL, 0);
